    "details": {
      "alignment": "Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "goblin"
      },
      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>The Regal Lion packet sheet — Warol Creeton.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-forge-packets.py</code> from the NPC Forge roster <code>data/forge/regal-lion.json</code> (entry <code>warol-creeton</code>): Small humanoid (goblin), Neutral; CR 1/2 (proficiency +2, to hit +4 with DEX); AC 14 (leather armor & steel buckler), hit points 18 (4d6+4), speed 30 ft.. A GM scene kit for the The Regal Lion article's present (1040 BF), not a filed event; the faction article stays the authority.</p><p>Stationed at the greenhouse perimeter, Warol greeted Byscilla's team with the crucial information that rust monsters spread faster in rain. Sensible enough to call for backup rather than get eaten.</p><p><strong>Role:</strong> perimeter sentry · <strong>tier:</strong> Greenhouse Sentry · <strong>folder:</strong> Iron Legion / Manor Wardens.</p><h3>Art</h3><p>Token plate <code>portraits/regal-lion/warol-creeton.png</code> — NPC Forge render, seed 610008, cut from a flat #FF00FF field. Prompt: <q>Clean cel-shaded character art in the style of dark fantasy military concept art, bold dark outlines, polished steel and gold lion crest heraldry, dark navy blue and crimson surcoats, cold iron plate, flat colours, crisp shading. A scrawny goblin sentry wearing an oversized steel kettle-hat helmet that covers his ears, an oilskin poncho protecting him from rain, holding a long spear with a rusted blade and a pouch of warning whistles. Full body, whole figure visible, three-quarter view, centred, isolated on a plain flat solid magenta background (#FF00FF), no floor, no ground shadow, no text, no border.</q></p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
